 # Decouple Chorus visual rendering from model-visible message injection
 
-
+Dogfood bug: if Chorus room messages arrive while an agent/session is mid-turn or the upstream provider stream is hung, the messages may not render in the main Pi chat until the turn boundary because the current custom message path queues through agent delivery. Evidence from Piper session: hung-period room posts were later found persisted as custom_message entries with customType chorus-room-message, display true, full XML content, and details, so this appears to be visual/live-render delay rather than transport loss. Need decouple immediate visual rendering from model-visible message injection.
